# `$hasContiguousIndex` finds an element in either storage of boxed values: whole numbers, or any values. The row in front of the copied loop of a list method asked for the second alone, and asked nothing at
# all of a list that is known to hold numbers: `[1, 2, 3, 4].forEach(..)` ran the copy of the loop that asks kind, pointer, length and bound in every turn. The row admits both now.
